1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,408
Good afternoon.

2
00:00:02,408 --> 00:00:08,581
My name’s Mrs Carter and I run the before and after school extended hours

3
00:00:08,581 --> 00:00:09,590
childcare service.

4
00:00:09,590 --> 00:00:13,597
I hope you’ve had a chance to have a good look around the school

5
00:00:13,597 --> 00:00:15,200
and talk to staff and pupils.

6
00:00:15,200 --> 00:00:19,977
I know that many of you are interested in using our childcare service when

7
00:00:19,977 --> 00:00:21,683
your child joins the school,

8
00:00:21,683 --> 00:00:24,413
and perhaps you already know something about it,

9
00:00:24,413 --> 00:00:29,190
but for those that don’t, I’ll go through the main details now.

10
00:00:29,190 --> 00:00:35,564
We offer childcare for children from the ages of four to eleven both before

11
00:00:35,564 --> 00:00:36,930
and after school.

12
00:00:36,930 --> 00:00:41,680
I know that many parents who work find this service invaluable.

13
00:00:41,680 --> 00:00:46,499
You can leave your child with us safe in the knowledge that they will

14
00:00:46,499 --> 00:00:48,220
be extremely well cared for.

15
00:00:48,220 --> 00:00:53,998
We are insured to provide care for up to 70 children, although we rarely

16
00:00:53,998 --> 00:00:57,300
have this many attending at any one session.

17
00:00:57,300 --> 00:01:03,315
I think we generally expect around 50–60 children for the afternoon sessions

18
00:01:03,315 --> 00:01:07,480
and about half that number for the breakfast sessions.

19
00:01:07,480 --> 00:01:13,722
Although we currently do have 70 children registered with us, not all of these

20
00:01:13,722 --> 00:01:15,060
attend every day.

21
00:01:15,060 --> 00:01:19,336
It’s ten years since we began offering an extended hours service

22
00:01:19,336 --> 00:01:22,900
and we’ve come a long way during that time.

23
00:01:22,900 --> 00:01:27,610
When we first opened, we only had about 20 children attending regularly.

24
00:01:27,610 --> 00:01:31,638
We try to keep our costs as low as we can

25
00:01:31,638 --> 00:01:35,300
and we think we provide very good value for money.

26
00:01:35,300 --> 00:01:36,959
For the afternoon sessions,

27
00:01:36,959 --> 00:01:42,350
which run from 3.30 until 6 p.m., it’s ￡7.20.

28
00:01:42,350 --> 00:01:47,320
But if you prefer, you can pay for one hour only,

29
00:01:47,320 --> 00:01:49,127
which costs ￡3.50,

30
00:01:49,127 --> 00:01:52,290
or two hours which costs ￡5.70.

31
00:01:52,290 --> 00:01:56,920
The cost of the childcare includes food and snacks.

32
00:01:56,920 --> 00:02:02,334
They’ll be given breakfast in the morning and in the afternoon, a healthy snack

33
00:02:02,334 --> 00:02:04,500
as soon as they finish school.

34
00:02:04,500 --> 00:02:06,232
At 5 p.m.

35
00:02:06,232 --> 00:02:11,430
children are given something more substantial, such as pasta or a casserole.

36
00:02:11,430 --> 00:02:15,715
Please inform us of any allergies that your child might have

37
00:02:15,715 --> 00:02:20,000
and we’ll make sure they’re offered a suitable alternative.

38
00:02:20,000 --> 00:02:25,250
As you may know, the childcare service runs through the school holidays from 8

39
00:02:25,250 --> 00:02:26,000
a.m.

40
00:02:26,000 --> 00:02:27,500
to 6 p.m.

41
00:02:27,500 --> 00:02:31,742
We offer a really varied and exciting programme to keep the children entertained –

42
00:02:31,742 --> 00:02:36,310
we don’t want them to feel as if they are still at school!

43
00:02:36,310 --> 00:02:41,710
It will also feel different because they’ll get the chance to make new friends

44
00:02:41,710 --> 00:02:45,310
with children from other schools – spaces are available for them

45
00:02:45,310 --> 00:02:50,350
because a lot of our term-time children don’t always attend during the holiday.

46
00:02:50,350 --> 00:02:55,352
In the past, parents have asked if children over the age of 11 are

47
00:02:55,352 --> 00:02:58,568
allowed to come with their younger brothers and sisters –

48
00:02:58,568 --> 00:03:04,285
but I’m afraid we’re unable to do this because of the type of insurance

49
00:03:04,285 --> 00:03:05,000
we have.

50
00:03:05,000 --> 00:03:10,425
So now let me tell you about some of the activities that your child

51
00:03:10,425 --> 00:03:12,750
can do during the afterschool sessions.

52
00:03:12,750 --> 00:03:16,997
As well as being able to use the playground equipment, computers

53
00:03:16,997 --> 00:03:22,402
and the library, there is usually at least one ‘special’ activity that children can

54
00:03:22,402 --> 00:03:23,560
do each day.

55
00:03:23,560 --> 00:03:25,930
For example, Spanish.

56
00:03:25,930 --> 00:03:33,023
We have a specialist teacher coming in every Thursday to give a basic introduction to the language through games

57
00:03:33,023 --> 00:03:33,770
and songs.

58
00:03:33,770 --> 00:03:35,309
She does two sessions:

59
00:03:35,309 --> 00:03:39,540
one for the over 8s and one for the younger children.

60
00:03:39,540 --> 00:03:44,384
This is the only activity which we have to make an extra charge for –

61
00:03:44,384 --> 00:03:46,460
but it’s well worth it.

62
00:03:46,460 --> 00:03:51,050
Once a week the children have the opportunity to do some music.

63
00:03:51,050 --> 00:03:55,400
We’re very lucky that one of our staff is a member of a folk

64
00:03:55,400 --> 00:03:55,690
band.

65
00:03:55,690 --> 00:04:00,970
On Mondays, she teaches singing and percussion to groups of children.

66
00:04:00,970 --> 00:04:03,630
We do rely on parental support for this,

67
00:04:03,630 --> 00:04:06,955
so if any of you sing or play an instrument

68
00:04:06,955 --> 00:04:11,610
and would be prepared to help out at these sessions, we’d be delighted.

69
00:04:11,610 --> 00:04:16,780
Painting continues to be one of the most popular activities.

70
00:04:16,780 --> 00:04:22,100
To begin with we weren’t keen on offering this because of the extra mess

71
00:04:22,100 --> 00:04:22,455
involved,

72
00:04:22,455 --> 00:04:26,357
but children kept asking if they could do some art and

73
00:04:26,357 --> 00:04:28,130
so we finally gave in.

74
00:04:28,130 --> 00:04:33,380
Art is great for helping the children to relax after working hard at school

75
00:04:33,380 --> 00:04:34,130
all day.

76
00:04:34,130 --> 00:04:38,402
Yoga is something that we’ve been meaning to introduce for some time

77
00:04:38,402 --> 00:04:43,003
but haven’t been able to find anyone available to teach it – until now

78
00:04:43,003 --> 00:04:43,660
that is.

79
00:04:43,660 --> 00:04:45,840
So we’ll see how this goes.

80
00:04:45,840 --> 00:04:51,030
Hopefully, children will benefit in all sorts of ways from this.

81
00:04:51,030 --> 00:04:54,020
Cooking is another popular activity.

82
00:04:54,020 --> 00:04:56,529
They make a different sort of cake,

83
00:04:56,529 --> 00:04:58,680
or pizza or bread each week.

84
00:04:58,680 --> 00:05:04,098
Although the younger children love doing it, we found that the mess was just

85
00:05:04,098 --> 00:05:04,872
too much,

86
00:05:04,872 --> 00:05:10,678
so we’ve decided to restrict this to the over 8s, as they are better

87
00:05:10,678 --> 00:05:13,000
able to clean up after themselves.
